                <pb facs="0510" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/1023.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Memorandum—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p>This embassy has private information to the effect that the I. C. Hirsch Iron,
                    Steel &amp; Rail Co., of Cincinnati, Ohio, whose address is International
                    Building, 226 East Fourth Street, holds a stock of 15,000 Springfield rifles and
                    125,000 cartridges and is ready to sell the rifles for $1.85, without, bayonet,
                    or $2.09, with bayonet and belt, and the cartridges for $24.15 a thousand, or
                    $21.40 for the whole lot. The factory announces that it has received offers for
                    the purchase of those arms.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Embassy of
                            Mexico</hi>,<lb/><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-18"><hi rendition="#italic">March 18,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
